geez gordo maybe pass on the 1500  glass of wine i wonder how many of those  speaking engagements he'd have to do  to buy a bottle like that have to say i  didn't see that move  coming and yeah that's a setup for his  time on the moon to be sure  hey guys pete here this is my for all  mankind  season 2 episode 6 breakdown it's titled  best laid plans  and as we move into the back half of the  season things are starting to come into  focus  we'll get into what those plans are  shaping up to be but first  let me give a quick spoiler warning if  you haven't watched episode 6 yet then  this will  absolutely spoil it for you hit the  subscribe button go watch it and then  come back  and with that out of the way let's jump  into it plot wise i really enjoyed the  soviet delegation coming to the us  i think it's been a thing sort of  hanging over this series  that there was never any perspective on  what was going on with the soviets  we only saw things from one perspective  and that's not necessarily a bad thing  because it does add to the tension of  all the interactions that they have with  each other  but in an alternate history situation  where we're expecting things to turn out  a different way  i think it does become necessary for us  to see their side of the story  and we've got these two parallel things  going on with them we have an escalation  of the cold war  we have the militarization of the moon  and the space program  in general but then we also have this  apollo soyuz thing  which on the surface is there to foster  goodwill  but as we see in this episode nobody  really  wants it to happen we get the pentagon's  perspective  they would be more than happy for things  to fall through as long as they're not  the ones with egg on their face  we can see that the official position of  the soviets is to not give an inch  and then we got danny in there she's  just happy to be in the room  she's just trying to make the most out  of her command  and then somewhat surprisingly thomas  paine  is really behind the idea for history's  sake which i guess somebody has to be  because it looks like this thing needs  to happen but both sides are more  interested in not giving anything away  not showing any weakness not making it  easy for the other side  and it looks like payne's our guy or at  least he's our guy to delegate things to  margot  which i will come back to i'll tell you  what though this is the second time they  showed us  a nicer side of pain showed that he  really cared about his job  that he wasn't just the politician  wasn't just the ear of the president  and i gotta say that puts up some red  flags i have to imagine that we're going  to see him lose his job  one way or the other that was one of the  big takeaways i had from this  and one of the other things that it made  me think about was as we see ellen  getting  closer to moving away from her position  and her working with him so closely i  hope there's not some kind of scandal or  something else that's going to come out  of that situation  either way to me it feels like they're  definitely setting something up with  thomas payne  it could be as simple as he gets pushed  out of the position in an election  but there's tension at the top around  this handshake in space  and that means margot has to figure out  a way to make it work  and that was mostly enjoyable to watch  we see that there's some chemistry going  on i think between her and sergey  they're both in a tough situation but  figure out a way to work together  elena gets caught up in that as well and  it seems like there might be an issue  with her supervisor bill who's a  familiar face that we've seen  throughout the entire run but in the end  they get the design to work  they present it everyone's happy sergey  acts like he wasn't involved in the  process  and then he breaks the stalemate with  the transmission codes by telling what  theirs is  first and pretty much everything's back  on track by the end of the episode  we get some good character moments as  danny and her crew member  hang out with the cosmonauts things  start off rough obviously  they go for burgers and you think maybe  that's gonna open the door  but there's still kind of a lot of  posturing going on  and then we see a slight break whenever  the soyuz commander  talks about the astronaut dog leica what  was interesting about that to me was  that they were  not really in agreement nobody changed  anybody else's mind really  but they still managed to connect on a  human level and i would guess that they  have a higher respect for each other  which is probably going to be necessary  as a result  danny's story ends with what almost felt  like a stinger at the very end of the  episode  when she arrives in russia with her  crewmate and they get a much  different reception we'll have to see  what's up with that in the next episode  though  because they never get past the  introduction so i opened up with gordo  and yep that's his plan he wants to go  back to the moon  and try to get tracy back i thought that  it was pretty interesting that we had  never seen  her husband on camera until this episode  and i guess he turns out to be what we  were expecting  he's the kind of guy who has bottles of  wine that thomas jefferson used to own  he's awfully confident and doesn't seem  too worried about gordo's plans  which could turn out bad for gordo let's  be honest  however it seems like he's been on this  path to overcome what happened the last  time so i'm not really sure how him  going back to the moon and then striking  out with tracy would really fit into  that  unless of course he is just heading for  a meltdown and always has been this  season we'll have to wait and see  either way it was a fun twist you kind  of saw it come to his mind  as he was overhearing his son talking to  tracy  and he went outside and sort of looked  up at the moon but i was still  pretty surprised to hear it come out of  his mouth tracy on the other hand  is starting to bond with the marines it  looks like and i guess that makes sense  she wasn't really fitting in with the  other astronauts because of her  celebrity status  and it looks like her skills at piloting  the lsam might come in handy  she's supposed to be training one of the  marines but he doesn't look like he's  very good at it yet  and that makes you wonder if she's not  going to be involved in whatever it is  they do  the only other thing that happened up  there was we do hear her talking with  deke again  she's kind of talking about she wants  something that lasts nothing on earth  lasts  almost sounds like she might be missing  gordo but really  is that where we're going i'm not sure  it seemed like they were going out of  their way to show that she was happy  with her new life then she goes to the  moon  we find out she's not that happy at  least not in that environment  and now her ex-husband who she hasn't  seemed all that interested in  lately is coming to try to win her over  elsewhere we do get a little bit of pam  and ellen we could see that ellen is all  in on this idea of getting back together  and not unsurprisingly pam doesn't trust  her  she doesn't want to throw everything  that she has right now away again  just to watch ellen not be able to pull  the trigger if you will  make a real commitment to the  relationship we see her go and talk to  larry  afterward and of course he's worried  about her coming out he doesn't really  want a divorce he likes the life they  have together  and you kind of feel a little bit bad  for him and it's one of those situations  that kind of hit because  neither one of them did anything wrong  here and his reasons for not wanting  things to end  isn't entirely selfish i think we still  have to imagine that if ellen is gonna  try to make this  a real relationship go public with it  then she's gonna experience a backlash  and will probably have to quit nasa  having said that you can still easily  understand her position  and understand why she might go that  direction she's in love that's all there  is to it really  beyond that we get a little bit of ed  and karen we see them watching a sea  dragon launch on the tv  and kelly's trying to write her letter  for the naval academy  and they get into this conversation  about why they  adopted her so it goes back to a real  thing that exists in our timeline and  that's  operation baby lift i'm not sure where  they're going bringing this up  at this point i think we'll see more  about that in the next episode  i think the big takeaway here for me was  that we get a little bit more insight  into how hard things were for them after  shane died  we find out that they were separated at  a time and that kelly played a key role  in them coming back together after they  adopted her  i'm not sure what's going on here i did  find it a little bit relieving that we  didn't see  any new interactions between danny and  karen  i was glad that we kind of didn't have  to go there we did see edit work we saw  him doing  a flight simulation with his pathfinder  crew  he looks like he's on top of his game as  far as that's concerned  his crew seems impressed things seem to  be moving along well  there and we'll just have to wait and  see what's going on at home  and how things develop ed and karen have  always come across as the kind of couple  that stay together no matter what  they have their problems as individuals  and as a couple  and they've dealt with their share of  tragedy most of that  has appeared to keep them together  though so it's hard to put together  something that i'd like to see happen  with them kelly's nearly an adult now  which means she'll be developing as an  independent character  who has her own arc in future seasons i  don't know i kind of like things as they  are there  ed had his moment earlier in the season  they were there for each other  karen's got the business now she seems  in her element there  maybe they don't need to be in the  center of things this season  i definitely like this episode better  than the last one  it feels like it's gaining some momentum  now always enjoy some focus on margot  and they put her in an interesting  position even brought some on-screen  chemistry into the mix you have to  imagine that her working with sergey  and then danny bonding with the soyuz  commander will be important later  because let's face it conflict is coming  not sure what to expect with gordo and  tracy or even when i want to come out of  that development to be honest  i guess hopefully it's just not extreme  to the point that they come back  together only for one of them to get  killed off right  i think that's a good place to leave  things let me know what you think about  where we are  and where we might be going probably not  a great sign that the marines completely  missed the target when they were trying  out their new guns so let me know what  you think about that  and anything else that's on your mind  about this season so far  because we are making our way towards  the end please like this video if you  enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already thanks for watching i'll  talk to you soon
 

